  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "mb_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Mic Bloom\n\nA flower that listens. Switch Microphone on and talk, sing, clap or play music near the computer: the petals are the spectrum (low notes at the top, high round the sides), the core swells with the bass, a beat sends a ring out and sparks fly with the treble. With the microphone off it listens to its own little demo loop (Demo volume sets how loud you hear it).\n\nHow it works: AudioIn and the demo (a MonoSynth arpeggio + noise hats) → Mix → FFT (64 bins). Expression turns the spectrum into 128 petal points mirrored left–right; Statistics (mean) of slices give bass and treble, Peak Detect finds beats. Without sound at all (no audio device) it breathes on a noise spectrum so it never goes dark. Echo smears it into trails.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
    {
